=== Sprint 25 idempotent-submit drill host=2026-08-04 ===

--- 1. Fix target: innermost live submission boundary (retry dup hazard) ---
Live chain: CycleExecutor -> JournaledBroker -> GuardrailedBroker ->
RateLimitedBroker -> AlpacaBrokerAdapter.submit_order (application/factory.py:182-223).
Adversary: adapter-internal retry_with_backoff(max_retries=2) re-submits after a
dropped response/timeout. If the broker accepted attempt #1 server-side, attempt
#2 creates a DUPLICATE order unless a stable client_order_id is reused.

--- 2. Changes (src/traderos/infrastructure/alpaca_broker.py) ---
- _new_client_order_id() helper (uuid4), generated once BEFORE the first submit
  attempt of a logical order and reused verbatim on every retry.
- client_order_id wired into: place_market_order (line 104), place_limit_order
  (146), place_stop_order (190), place_trailing_stop_order (234) request
  objects, inside their _submit closures (retry boundary at lines 108/150/194/238).
- Optional client= injection seam added to __init__ for tests.
- EXCLUDED: modify_order (replace_order_by_id, line ~260) - alpaca-py
  ReplaceOrderRequest has no client_order_id field; not applicable.

--- 3. Proof: real CycleExecutor -> real AlpacaBrokerAdapter -> fake Alpaca client ---
Fake server semantics: FIRST submit of a new client_order_id records the order
server-side, then drops the response (TimeoutError). Retry with the SAME
client_order_id returns the existing order (no duplicate).

  >>> TEST 1: timeout-after-record creates EXACTLY ONE order
      attempts=2, server-side orders=1, retry reused same client_order_id
